> We are not allowed to acquire other locks within LOCK_KEYS(). The referenced commit violates that locking discipline, which leads to deadlock.

I confirm that thread 36 holds `LOCK_KEYS()` lock and then tries to acquire `BEGIN_TYPE_LOCK()` while calling `PyType_Modified()`:

```
Thread 36 (Thread 0x7fff8c1f96c0 (LWP 897490) "test_ABC_helper"):
...
#9  0x0000000000726a00 in _PyMutex_Lock (m=m@entry=0xc3e1d8 <_PyRuntime+371352>) at ./Include/cpython/pylock.h:56
#10 0x0000000000726c53 in _PyCriticalSection_BeginSlow (tstate=tstate@entry=0x7fffb210a010, c=c@entry=0x7fff8c1f6d00, m=m@entry=0xc3e1d8 <_PyRuntime+371352>) at Python/critical_section.c:59
#11 0x00000000005d4972 in _PyCriticalSection_BeginMutex (tstate=tstate@entry=0x7fffb210a010, c=c@entry=0x7fff8c1f6d00, m=0xc3e1d8 <_PyRuntime+371352>) at ./Include/internal/pycore_critical_section.h:115
#12 0x00000000005e4825 in PyType_Modified (type=0x7fffb52f2d10) at Objects/typeobject.c:1250
    BEGIN_TYPE_LOCK();
#13 0x000000000056fd1a in _PyDict_SplitKeysInvalidated (keys=keys@entry=0x7fffb52c1f98) at Objects/dictobject.c:7179
#14 0x000000000056fe22 in insert_split_key (keys=keys@entry=0x7fffb52c1f98, key=key@entry='expected', hash=-7841562925341399119) at Objects/dictobject.c:1930
    LOCK_KEYS(keys);
    ix = unicodekeys_lookup_unicode(keys, key, hash);
    if (ix == DKIX_EMPTY && keys->dk_usable > 0) {
        // Insert into new slot
        FT_ATOMIC_STORE_UINT32_RELAXED(keys->dk_version, 0);
        _PyDict_SplitKeysInvalidated(keys);  // <==== HERE
```

The "referenced commit" Sam's talking about is this one: https://github.com/python/cpython/commit/efb2fffae1fc728a5467672e6781cdf2df9bfec3.  The lock being acquired inside `LOCK_KEYS()` is done by the call to `PyType_Modified()`.  Possible solution is to move the invalidation out of the LOCK_KEYS region. E.g. something like this:

```
static Py_ssize_t
insert_split_key(PyDictKeysObject *keys, PyObject *key, Py_hash_t hash)
{
    assert(PyUnicode_CheckExact(key));
    Py_ssize_t ix;
#ifdef Py_GIL_DISABLED
    ix = unicodekeys_lookup_unicode_threadsafe(keys, key, hash);
    if (ix >= 0) {
        return ix;
    }
#endif
    bool inserted = false;
    LOCK_KEYS(keys);
    ix = unicodekeys_lookup_unicode(keys, key, hash);
    if (ix == DKIX_EMPTY && keys->dk_usable > 0) {
        FT_ATOMIC_STORE_UINT32_RELAXED(keys->dk_version, 0);
        Py_ssize_t hashpos = find_empty_slot(keys, hash);
        ix = keys->dk_nentries;
        dictkeys_set_index(keys, hashpos, ix);
        PyDictUnicodeEntry *ep = &DK_UNICODE_ENTRIES(keys)[ix];
        STORE_SHARED_KEY(ep->me_key, Py_NewRef(key));
        split_keys_entry_added(keys);
        inserted = true;
    }
    assert (ix < SHARED_KEYS_MAX_SIZE);
    UNLOCK_KEYS(keys);
    if (inserted) {
        _PyDict_SplitKeysInvalidated(keys);  // <-- PyType_Modified() called inside here
    }
    return ix;
}
```
